"Coxen Hole is the largest city on the island of Roatán, and the capital of the Bay Islands department of Honduras, with a population of 8,307 as of the 2021 census. It is also the location of the island's Juan Manuel Gálvez International Airport.","wpu":"Coxen Hole","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Port_Roatan_Coxen_Hole_Roatan_Honduras_2026.jpg/960px-Port_Roatan_Coxen_Hole_Roatan_Honduras_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Aerolínea Lanhsa Flight 018","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":16.316611,"lo":-86.51975,"d":1841,"ds":"Aerolínea Lanhsa Flight 018 was a charter flight on 17 March 2025, from Juan Manuel Gálvez International Airport, on Roatán Island, department of Islas de la Bahía, to Golosón International Airport in La Ceiba, department of Atlántida.","wpu":"Aerolínea Lanhsa Flight 018","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/British_Aerospace_Jetstream_31%2C_Lanhsa_%28Linea_Aerea_Nacional_de_Honduras_S.A.%29_JP11233383.jpg/960px-British_Aerospace_Jetstream_31%2C_Lanhsa_%28Linea_Aerea_Nacional_de_Honduras_S.A.%29_JP11233383.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Roatán (Spanish pronunciation: [ro.aˈtan]) is an island in the Caribbean, about 65 kilometres (40 mi) off the northern coast of Honduras. The largest of the Bay Islands of Honduras, it is located between the islands of Utila and Guanaja. It is approximately 59 kilometres (37 mi) long, and less than 8 kilometres (5.0 mi) across at its widest point.","wpu":"Roatán","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/Westbay2106.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}